  "id": "Compound::DB00687 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fludrocortisone and Nr3c1, mediated through the shared interaction with Prednisolone or Methylprednisolone. Both Fludrocortisone and Prednisolone bind to Nr3c1, which is a steroid receptor involved in the regulation of electrolyte balance and glucocorticoid signaling. The presence of a common ancestor, 3-Oxo-Delta(4) Steroid, indicates a shared biosynthetic pathway, reinforcing the possibility of a common mechanism of action. The evidence also highlights that Fludrocortisone may influence Nr3c1 through its role in causing alkalosis hypokalaemia, which is associated with increased insulin requirement, further suggesting a systemic impact on glucocorticoid signaling. The scores from the paths are consistent, indicating a strong and reliable relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
